# DTF tier manifest: proxy-stale-if-error  (artifact-keeper#4581 / PR #4697,
# with #4640 / PR #4783)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the steerable static upstream (upstreams.mock-static,
# harness/tiers/proxy-cache-empty-object/fixtures/mock_static.py). This tier
# adds four per-path modes to that mock: e500, e404, e410 (answer that status)
# and stall (hold the request 75 s, then answer ok); HEAD honours them too.
#
# THE FIX (#4581)
# A Remote revalidates a mutable cache entry past its TTL. When the upstream
# answers 5xx, times out or fails in transport, the proxy serves the stale body
# under RFC 5861 stale-if-error for a grace window past expiry. Before #4697
# that window was a hard-coded 3600 s and a stale serve looked exactly like a
# fresh one. #4697:
#   * marks a stale serve with `Warning: 110 - "Response is stale"` and
#     `X-AK-Stale-Since: <RFC 3339 expiry>`, counts it in
#     ak_proxy_stale_if_error_responses_total{repo} and remembers it
#     (last_stale_served_at);
#   * makes the grace configurable: PROXY_STALE_IF_ERROR_GRACE_SECS (default
#     3600, 0..2592000) and per Remote via
#     PUT/GET /api/v1/repositories/{key}/stale-if-error-grace
#     ({"stale_if_error_grace_seconds": N}); past the grace the upstream error
#     is returned instead of the stale body;
#   * leaves a fresh hit, a 304-confirmed body and a copy kept under
#     on_upstream_not_found=keep (#4640, PR #4783) unmarked. The last one is the
#     merge fix: a kept copy after a definitive 404/410 is not stale-if-error.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   Generic paths are mutable (cache_classifier: default formats), so a Remote
#   with cache_ttl_seconds=2 expires an entry 2 s after it is cached. The
#   oracle primes an entry, waits out the TTL, flips the mock path to an error
#   mode and GETs again.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      grace API (default 3600, PUT/GET round trip, 400 out of range,
#              Remote only); upstream 500 inside the default grace -> 200 stale
#              body + both markers + the counter + last_stale_served_at;
#              upstream stall past the proxy's 60 s read timeout -> the same;
#              a 6 s per-repo grace -> stale + markers inside it, the upstream
#              error (503) past it; with on_upstream_not_found=keep an upstream
#              404 / 410 serves the kept copy with NO markers, counted as kept
#              and not as stale.
#              RED on 1.11.3: no markers, no counter, no grace route (404),
#              stale served past any short grace, no on-upstream-not-found
#              route. On main 03edc6e6 (#4783 without #4697) every #4581 case
#              is red and the keep case is green.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: a cold fetch caches and the next fetch
#              is a hit, neither marked; under the default policy an upstream
#              404 on an expired entry answers 404, not the old body.
#   (FIX #4815) RED on main 2f08663f, GREEN from main adfa0206: the grace GET
#              on a private Remote is 404 to an anonymous and to a no-grant
#              caller (it had no visibility check and answered 200).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~50 authenticated calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-static"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
